## Q11 (gui-stack-v1-issues) — destructuring tuple bindings in a `for` over a
## Hash (and an Array of pairs). The value binding (`scopes`) used to stay an
## inference variable all the way into codegen (mangled `?T_remove`); now the
## for-loop propagates the `(K, V)` element type to the sub-bindings so method
## calls on them resolve.

def main
  var subs: Hash[Int, Set[Int]] = Hash.new
  var s: Set[Int] = Set.new
  s.insert(7)
  s.insert(9)
  subs.insert(1, s)
  for (sid, scopes) in &subs
    scopes.remove(7)
    puts "sid=#{sid} size=#{scopes.size}"
  end

  let pairs: Array[(Int, Int)] = [(1, 10), (2, 20)]
  for (n, m) in pairs
    puts "#{n}:#{m}"
  end
end
